        <definition>void Camera2D::Update</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>Update</name>
        <qualifiedname>Camera2D::Update</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Updates the view matrix if the camera is dirty. Should be called before rendering if the camera has moved or rotated. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Updates the view matrix ONLY when the camera is dirty.</para>
<para>The view matrix is the inverse of the camera&apos;s transform:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Apply translation to -position</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Apply rotation around Z-axis (inverse angle) </para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
