    <briefdescription>
<para>2D camera with orthographic projection, position, rotation, and zoom. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classCamera2D" kindref="compound">Camera2D</ref> class manages an orthographic projection matrix and a view matrix based on the camera&apos;s position, rotation (around Z-axis), and zoom level. It is used to define what part of the world is visible on screen.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>The camera uses a dirty flag to avoid recalculating the view matrix every frame unless the position or rotation has changed. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
